.TH TULPAR-LIST 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.2.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-list \- list installed packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar list
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ pattern ]
.br
.B tulpar l
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ pattern ]
.br
.B tulpar \-l
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ pattern ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Lists packages recorded in the package database, with their
installed version and hold state. When an optional
.I pattern
substring is provided, only installed packages whose name contains the
pattern are displayed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
List the database of an alternate root.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-json
Print the package list as a JSON array instead of human-readable
text.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-search (1),
.BR tulpar-info (1)
